# Intro
A single star at the center of a uniform, periodic gas box, with only the
radiation-pressure momentum channel active. Photoionization, cooling and
gravity are all off. Compares the shell the star's radiation pressure drives
outward against the momentum-conserving analytic solution of Krumholz &
Matzner (2009, ApJ 703, 1352), radiation-only limit: `R(t) = [3 f_trap
L_bol t^2 / (2 pi rho_0 c)]^(1/4)`, with `f_trap` this code's own
`(1-exp(-tau_NUV))*(1+tau_IR)`.

Formula-level correctness of the momentum-injection rate itself (Eq.
rp-momentum-rate in `theory/GEAR/Radiation/01_radiation_pressure.tex`) is
covered separately by `tests/testRadiationPressureFormula.c`, with no hydro
involved: a gas-kinematics comparison cannot isolate the formula from the
gas's own hydrodynamical response to the kick, which is exactly what this
example measures instead.

## Density and metallicity
`gas_density` defaults to `1e3 cm^-3`: dense enough for the shell to grow
measurably within an affordable run, while keeping the box large enough
that the shell stays inside it for the whole comparison window.
`GEARChemistry:initial_metallicity` is solar (`1`, i.e. `Z/Zsun=1`).

## f_trap is measured, not assumed
`f_trap` depends on the star's own local gas column, which changes as
radiation pressure empties the region around it. The check script reads it
directly from each snapshot's `EnrichmentWeight`/`GradRhoStar`/`ZStar`
star fields and reports how much it drifts over the run, rather than
assuming it stays at its literature fiducial value. Those fields only
exist in a build configured with `--enable-debug-interactions-stars` (see
Configure below) -- without it, the check script raises an error asking
for a rebuild.

## SPH:h_max
The star's own smoothing length grows as its local neighbourhood empties
out, and is otherwise unbounded (`SPH:h_max` defaults to `FLT_MAX`).
`run.sh` computes and sets it from the run's own box size (just under
`(boxsize/3)/kernel_gamma`, this example's cell-grid limit) to avoid a
`cell_set_spart_h_depth()` crash once the shell has grown enough to matter.

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_1 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle --enable-debug-interactions-stars=64
make -j
```

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Override any parameter via the matching env var, e.g. `gas_density=1e5 ./run.sh` -- see `run.sh` for the full list.

# Checking
```
python3 radiation_pressure_shell_expansion_check.py
```
Tracks the simulated shell radius two ways (a Lagrangian-mass radius, the
primary metric matched to the analytic model's own thin-shell accounting;
a density-peak radius, a secondary audit diagnostic), compares the primary
one against the analytic curve over the run's box-valid window, and
reports PASS/FAIL against a median relative-error tolerance (`--tol`,
default 25%). Produces a comparison plot (`--output`, default
`shell_expansion_check.png`).
